# LEXOS Testing and Acceptance Rules

Do not claim completion without running available checks.

Use:

`docs/implementation/04 MVP Acceptance Test Plan.md`

as the MVP acceptance authority.

Every work packet must include either automated tests or a manual verification report.

The MVP fails if:

- Evidence Extraction Object is missing;
- Support Matrix is missing;
- unsupported facts are hidden;
- contradictions are hidden;
- W9 is skipped;
- raw OCR-only screenshot extraction is silently accepted;
- retrieval is global by default;
- workflow state is missing;
- artifact status is missing;
- audit events are missing for material actions;
- original evidence can be overwritten by extraction;
- embeddings are treated as evidence;
- rejected/abandoned W0 intake becomes persistent W1 client memory.

W4-lite acceptance requires:

- Evidence Object;
- Evidence Extraction Object;
- original preserved unchanged;
- markdown extraction where applicable;
- structured JSON extraction where applicable;
- `processing_status`;
- `extraction_quality_status`;
- `human_review_required`;
- quality flags;
- no silent reliance on failed/QA-flagged extraction.

Before final report, include:

- commands run;
- test/manual verification results;
- known failures;
- unresolved risks;
- whether acceptance criteria were met.

If tests fail and cannot be fixed within the assigned work packet, stop and report the failure rather than broadening scope.
